  "description": "A Chauvet Rogue R2 Spot, a single-head moving spot, probably about 28 by 44 by 16 cm overall. A rectangular base holds the fixed housing and control panel and carries a U-shaped yoke whose arms form the tilt axis. The head is a rounded barrel with one flat, round front lens disc about six units across. Behind it sits one LED engine, giving a single emitter, one circular cell and one controllable intensity cell. Pan turns the yoke about the vertical axis through roughly 540 degrees, and tilt swings the head between the yoke arms through about 270 degrees, both DMX driven. Wheels, prism, and iris, frost, shutter, strobe and focus lack geometry and need parameters.",
